  "macroTheme": "Warsh FOMC hawkish hold Jun 17: dot plot flips with 9/18 members projecting a 2026 hike, easing bias removed. Gold almost hit 4,150 target (low 4,139). NAS100 quad-witching surge +2.48% on Jun 18 distorted the hawkish signal. UK CPI missed consensus. ECB Sintra Jun 24-25 is the next major catalyst.",
  "macroOverview": "The FOMC on June 17 delivered a unanimous hold at 3.50-3.75% but the dot plot shifted hawkish: 9 of 18 members project at least one rate hike before end 2026. Warsh replaced easing bias language with 'The Committee will deliver price stability.' Gold and silver crashed post-announcement; XAUUSD target 4,150 was delivered (low 4,139 on Juneteenth Friday). UK CPI May came in at 2.8% headline (below 3.0% consensus), stopping out the GBPCAD long. US Retail Sales May +0.9% MoM validated the hawkish backdrop. NAS100 quad-witching expiration (rolled from Juneteenth Fri to Thu Jun 18) generated record volume and a +2.48% squeeze that stopped out the NAS100 short. US30 printed a new year-to-date ATH of 52,281 before reversing on the hawkish FOMC. ECB Sintra Forum June 24-25 is the key near-term event for GER40 and EUR pairs. US PCE May on June 26 is the dominant end-of-week catalyst.",
